Ireland &#8216;s VFX industry is attempting to capitalize on the introduction of an enhanced 40% tax credit, which offers qualifying international productions opportunities to undertake large-scale visual effects work in the country.

&#8220;I'm delighted to return to SSVFX at such an exciting time for the studio and the wider Irish VFX industry,&#8221; said Thompson. &#8220;I've always admired the ambition, artistry and collaborative spirit of the team, and it's a privilege to be part of its next chapter.

She boards a leadership team at SSVFX that also includes VFX Supervisor Donal Nolan, who joined earlier this year and was a former Creative Head of Studio at Milk VFX in Dublin. He leads the studio's creative operation alongside longstanding SSVFX VFX Supervisor Ronan Gantly, and the team also includes Head of Production Ciar&#xE1;n Keenan.

Jake Walshe, CEO of the Screen Scene Group, said: &#8220;We are delighted to welcome Jennifer back to SSVFX. She knows our people, our culture and what makes this studio special. Together with Donal, Ronan and Ciar&#xE1;n, we've brought together an exceptional depth of creative and production leadership, with experience spanning some of the world's most respected VFX facilities and ambitious international productions. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dl-mid-article-inject2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article2","mid-articleX","mid-article","mid","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#8220;We've built a studio in Dublin with a reputation for delivering world-class visual effects, and the strength of this team gives us an exciting opportunity to build on that success. Our focus is on deepening our relationships with filmmakers and production partners, bringing more ambitious projects to Ireland and continuing to develop the extraordinary talent we have here.&#8221;

Thompson added: &#8220;With an incredible depth of creative talent, experienced production leadership and new opportunities opening up for Ireland internationally, we're in a fantastic position to build new partnerships, embrace emerging technologies and take on even bigger and more ambitious projects.&#8221;

Dark comedy &#8220; We Are Born Good ,&#8221; which leads this year's Hong Kong contenders at the Golden Horse Awards with nine nominations, has been picked up for the U.K. by Trinity CineAsia .

The distributor secured rights from Edko Films and will open the film in British cinemas on Dec. 4.

The film is the feature directing debut of Yeung Leung Chuen, who wrote &#8220;Hong Kong Family.&#8221; Golden Horse winner Chung Suet Ying (&#8220;The Way We Talk&#8221;) stars opposite Yeung Wai Lun (&#8220;The Sparring Partner&#8221;). The supporting cast includes Lo Chun Yip (&#8220;Time Still Turns the Pages&#8221;), Kearen Pang (&#8220;Mama's Affair&#8221;), Ng Wing Sze (&#8220;Mad Fate&#8221;) and Yan Yuk Yu Amy (Echaluce) (&#8220;Night King&#8221;). blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Benjamín Vicuña, Star of Netflix Hit Series 'Envious,' Joins ‘My Last Stand' by Goya-Winner Matías Bize Oscars: International Feature — ‘La Bola Negra,’ ‘Fjord’ and 'Minotaur' Lead Early Contenders

At the 63rd Golden Horse Awards, the film is up for best narrative feature, leading actor, leading actress, new director and original screenplay, among other categories. It world premiered at Toronto, then traveled to Zurich for its European bow and Pingyao for its Asian launch. It opened in Hong Kong theaters on Oct. 29.

Yeung took his starting point from a CCTV clip that went viral, in which a petty quarrel between a market vendor and a customer turned violent. Rather than dwell on the clash itself, the film digs into what drives people in present-day Hong Kong to snap: money worries, job stress, family duty and social bias, piling up with no release valve. Nobody is painted as a villain. Instead, the story tracks how fury and burnout can tip otherwise decent people into trouble.

Zoey, a rising actor drowning in debt, sets out to get even after a restaurant botches her order and refuses to cook a replacement because it's past closing time. Wing-kat, who runs the place, has his own problems &#x2013; he's only just out of prison. What starts as a minor spat becomes a running feud as both their lives come apart. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

The project came out of Hong Kong's First Feature Film Initiative. GoodNight Production produced, with Patricia Cheng as producer. The film runs 96 minutes and is in Cantonese.

Cedric Behrel, managing director of Trinity CineAsia, said: &#8220;Following our release of &#8216;Hong Kong Family' in North America in 2022, written by Leung Chuen Yeung; we are proud to continue supporting his work by bringing his feature debut &#8216;We Are Born Good' to U.K. audiences, in partnership with our long-time friends at Edko Films. It combines sharp entertainment with genuine emotional depth and establishes Yeung as an exciting emerging filmmaker in East Asian cinema. With its strong festival presence and award recognition, we look forward to strengthening the international reach of contemporary Hong Kong cinema.&#8221;

Trinity CineAsia's recent U.K. and European releases include Bi Gan's Cannes special prize winner &#8220;Resurrection,&#8221; global animation box office champ &#8220;Ne Zha 2,&#8221; Jackie Chan crime actioner &#8220;The Shadow's Edge&#8221; and Teochew-language breakout &#8220;Dear You.&#8221;

Czech-Slovak drama Intimacy on Prescription won the main prize at the TV Beats Co-Financing Market of Industry@Tallinn & Baltic Event (ITBE) , the market of the Tallinn Black Nights Film Festival (P&#xD6;FF) in Estonia, whose 30th edition runs through this weekend.

A total of four awards were handed out to the most promising series projects of the 2026 edition of the event (its sixth in total).

The TV Beats Co-Financing Market brought together 10 series projects, originating from Czechia, Estonia, Finland, Lithuania, Ireland, Spain, Belgium, Poland, and Iceland, to be co-developed in collaboration with other European countries. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4],[300,251]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Movies 'You Can See Everything' Cinematographer on Billy Evans' Nude Scene and Tension Between Him and the Team General News From Venice Winner 'Woman Unknown' and Westeros to 'Star City': Meet Some of the Baltic Craft Specialists Who've Worked on Int'l Productions

The main prize is the &#x20AC;50,000 ($55,000) Council of Europe Series Co-Production Development Award. Intimacy on Prescription is directed by Ji&#x159;&#xED; Havelka, written by Kristina M&#xE1;jov&#xE1; and produced by Luk&#xE1;&#x161; Gargul&#xE1;k and Karolina Zalabakova of Cinebonbon. The jury praised the project's &#8220;originality, universal theme, fresh perspective on 1970s Eastern European society and thorough research.&#8221;

&#8220;Can good sex save every marriage?&#8221; reads a synopsis of the show. &#8220;In 1970s Czechoslovakia, two therapists try to prove it.&#8221;

Here is more on the series: &#8220;An experimental residential sex therapy unit opens inside a psychiatric clinic in Krom&#x11B;&#x159;&#xED;&#x17E;. Married couples arrive for a two-week stay hoping to save relationships that have stopped working at home and in bed. Each case begins as a sexual problem, but gradually reveals deeper wounds: shame, power, fear, trauma and the longing to be understood. At the center stand charismatic sexologist Franti&#x161;ek Muller and precise psychologist Petra T&#xE1;nsk&#xE1;, whose methods clash as much as they complement each other. As the clinic becomes an island of openness in a rigid society, the doctors' own lives begin to fall apart.&#8221; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Meanwhile, the MIDPOINT Talent Award was presented to the Belgian psychological thriller series The Inheritance , written by Alexandra Jans and Jan Van Dyck and produced by Kristoffel Mertens, Kato Maes and Karlijn Van de Cruys of Panenka. The award offers in-depth script development guidance from an experienced MIDPOINT Institute mentor.

Here's the synopsis for the show: &#8220;To save her struggling animal shelter, Hanne lies her way into the wealthy hunting family of the father she never knew, searching for the missing will that could change everything.&#8221;

The Irish-Canadian series Tanner , produced by F&#xED;b&#xED;n Films and Rhombus Media, received two awards: the TV Drama Vision Select Award, giving it visibility at TV Drama Vision in Gothenburg in 2027, and the Conecta 2027 Award.

The synopsis for this project is short and to the point, reading: &#8220;A former intelligence officer's search for a missing boy exposes a threat to democracy itself.&#8221;

Indian star Tabu , whose international credits include &#8220;Life of Pi&#8221; and &#8220; Dune: Prophecy ,&#8221; has signed on to &#8220; Tunnel Men ,&#8221; a Netflix series from YRF Entertainment, the streaming banner of studio Yash Raj Films.

The show is her first original Hindi-language series for streaming.

&#8220;Tunnel Men&#8221; is a fictionalized drama that takes its cue from the 2023 rescue in the northern Indian state of Uttarakhand. That November, a tunnel collapse left a group of workers trapped underground, and India watched anxiously as the effort to free them dragged on. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Producer Accused of 'Laughing' During Russell Brand Assault 'Steps Back' From Head of Comedy Role ‘Russell Brand: Open Secret’: Netflix Doc Reveals His ‘Jokes’ About Rape, Making a Girlfriend ‘Brush Her Teeth Until They Bled’ and More

The series sets out to capture the grit and cooperation that carried the operation through. &#8220;The Railway Men&#8221; director Shiv Rawail is back on board as showrunner.

Over a career of more than 30 years, Tabu has moved freely between commercial and independent cinema, working in Hindi as well as in regional-language films. She won Indian National Film Awards for &#8220;Maachis&#8221; and &#8220;Chandni Bar,&#8221; while &#8220;Maqbool,&#8221; &#8220;Haider&#8221; and &#8220;Andhadhun&#8221; proved her versatility.

Outside India, she played Ashima Ganguli in Mira Nair's &#8220;The Namesake,&#8221; appeared in Ang Lee's &#8220;Life of Pi&#8221; and took on the role of Sister Francesca in the series &#8220;Dune: Prophecy.&#8221;

